-- title:
--   Extending a Hecke point from level S to S₀
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field, let $p$ be an odd prime lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, i.e. a two-dimensional vector space $V$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ to $\mathrm{End}(V)$ trivial on a finite-level subgroup, assumed absolutely irreducible (its base change to an algebraic closure of the residue field has no invariant submodule other than $\bot$ and $\top$). Let $S_0 \subseteq S$ be finite sets of primes with $p \in S$, and $N \ge 1$ such that every prime divisor of $N$ lies in $S$ and not in $S_0$, and such that $\bar\rho$ fails to be unramified at every prime $q \ne p$ with $q \parallel N$; assume the weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ are spanned over $\mathbb C$ by the $\mathbb Z$-span of those with integral $q$-expansion coefficients. Let $\theta' : \mathbb T^{S_0} \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$ be a ring homomorphism on the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the $T_\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S_0$ and the $U_q$ with $q \mid N$, $q \notin S_0$) subject to: for $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S_0$, $\ell \ne p$, and any valuation subring $P$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ in which $\ell$ is a nonunit and any $\sigma$ acting on the residue field of $P$ as $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - \theta'(T_\ell)X + \ell$; $\theta'(U_q) = 0$ when $q^2 \mid N$; and $\theta'(U_q)$ for $q \parallel N$, resp. $\theta'(T_p)$ when $p \nmid N$ and $p \notin S_0$, equals the trace of any endomorphism of the inertia coinvariants $V/\sum_{\tau \in I_P}\mathrm{im}(\bar\rho(\tau)-1)$ induced by such a $\sigma$. Let $\theta$ be the composite of $\theta'$ with the inclusion of [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) into [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18). Finally let $\mathcal O'$ be a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field which is a module-finite $\mathcal O$-algebra with injective local structure map, and let $\chi : \mathbb T^{S} \to \mathcal O'$ be a ring homomorphism whose reduction is the image of $\theta$ in $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O'$. Then there is a further such ring $\mathcal O''$, a module-finite $\mathcal O'$-algebra with injective local structure map, and a ring homomorphism $\chi' : \mathbb T^{S_0} \to \mathcal O''$ extending $\chi$ (its restriction along the inclusion is $\chi$ followed by $\mathcal O' \to \mathcal O''$) and reducing to the image of $\theta'$ in $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O''$.
--
--   This is Lemma 4.6 of Darmon–Diamond–Taylor phrased in terms of points of Hecke algebras: a homomorphism of the Hecke algebra away from $S$ whose reduction is the residual eigensystem cut out by $\bar\rho$ extends, after a finite extension of the coefficient ring, to the larger Hecke algebra away from $S_0$, with prescribed reduction. It is used in the bound on the rank of the localised Hecke algebra, [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.finrank_le_of_subset_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.finrank_le_of_subset_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq).
